# The ledger of `openapi`: what the OpenAPI libraries of Go, Rust and Python
# let a program do, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers. None
# of the three standard libraries speaks OpenAPI, so the yardstick is the
# census the author chose on 2026-11-17, measured on this machine on
# 2026-11-18: Go's `github.com/getkin/kin-openapi` v0.153.0 (`openapi3`,
# `openapi3filter`, `routers`, `routers/gorillamux`, `routers/legacy`,
# `openapi3gen`, `openapi2conv`), `github.com/swaggo/swag` v1.16.6 and
# `github.com/swaggo/echo-swagger` v1.5.2 (`go doc -all`, the modules fetched
# into the scratch folder's module cache); Python's `fastapi` 0.165.0
# (`fastapi.openapi.*`, `fastapi.params`, `fastapi.security`), `openapi-core`
# 0.23.1, `openapi-spec-validator` 0.8.5 and `openapi-schema-validator` 0.8.1
# (`dir()`, installed into the scratch folder with pip); Rust's `utoipa`,
# `utoipa-swagger-ui` and `aide`, their items read from docs.rs's list of
# each crate (no crate is built on this machine).
#
# The references the tests were held to, asked on 2026-11-18: openapi-core
# 0.23.1 for routing, parameters, bodies, security, defaults and responses
# (27 requests and 6 responses of the store of pets, `fixture.pets_yaml`);
# kin-openapi 0.153.0 for every parameter style (23 requests of
# `fixture.styles_yaml`); openapi-spec-validator 0.8.5 for documents broken
# one rule at a time (20 cases) and for the full document,
# `fixture.full_yaml`; FastAPI 0.165.0 for the pages of Swagger UI and Redoc.
#
# Measured on 2026-11-18: the driver `examples-rebel/reach_openapi.hero`,
# built, prints a document openapi-spec-validator finds valid and openapi-core
# loads, and with `--serve` answers its document as JSON and YAML, both
# pages, a valid request 200, a request its document refuses 400 with a
# problem of RFC 9457, an unknown path 404 and a method its path does not
# take 405 with `Allow`.

capability document/build  an OpenAPI 3.1 document built as data by functions, every field set directly
  heroes  openapi.Document, openapi.new_document, openapi.OPENAPI_VERSION, openapi.DIALECT_URI
  go      openapi3.T, openapi3.T.AddOperation, openapi3.T.AddServer, openapi3.T.AddServers, openapi3.T.Extensions, openapi3.IsOpenAPI31OrLater, openapi3.IsOpenAPI32OrLater, openapi3.Ptr, openapi3.BoolPtr, openapi3.Float64Ptr, openapi3.Int64Ptr, openapi3.Uint64Ptr
  rust    utoipa openapi::OpenApi, OpenApiBuilder, OpenApiVersion, Modify, aide openapi::OpenApi, TransformOpenApi
  python  fastapi.openapi.models.OpenAPI, fastapi.openapi.utils.get_openapi, fastapi.openapi.constants.REF_PREFIX, REF_TEMPLATE, METHODS_WITH_BODY
  note    No document is derived from a program's types: the language has no reflection, so the program builds the data utoipa's derives and FastAPI's models would; a field left empty, false or null is not written

capability document/info  the API's title, summary, description, terms, contact, licence and version
  heroes  openapi.Info, openapi.Contact, openapi.License, openapi.new_contact, openapi.new_license
  go      openapi3.Info, openapi3.Contact, openapi3.License
  rust    utoipa openapi::info::Info, InfoBuilder, Contact, ContactBuilder, License, LicenseBuilder, aide openapi::Info, Contact, License
  python  fastapi.openapi.models.Info, Contact, License, FastAPI(title=, summary=, description=, version=, terms_of_service=, contact=, license_info=)

