capability check/document  a document checked against what OpenAPI 3.1 asks beyond each object's form, every problem with its pointer
  heroes  openapi.errors_of, openapi.check, openapi.Problem
  go      openapi3.T.Validate, openapi3.ValidationOption, openapi3.ValidationOptions, openapi3.ValidateIdentifier, openapi3.MultiError, openapi3.CodedError, openapi3.ValidationErrorCodes, openapi3.EnableMultiError, openapi3.FailFast, openapi3.ConflictingPathsError, openapi3.DuplicateOperationIDError, openapi3.DuplicateParameterError, openapi3.DuplicateTagError, openapi3.PathParametersError, openapi3.PathParameterRequiredError, openapi3.SecurityRequirementSchemeUndefinedError, openapi3.ServerURLUndeclaredVariables, openapi3.ServerURLUnusedVariables, openapi3.ServerVariableDefaultRequired, openapi3.InvalidParameterInError, openapi3.InvalidSerializationMethodError, openapi3.ComponentValidationError and every other error type of `openapi3` ending in Error, Required, Forbidden, Exclusive or FieldFor31Plus
  rust    -
  python  openapi_spec_validator.validate, validate_spec, OpenAPIV31SpecValidator, OpenAPIV3SpecValidator, openapi_v31_spec_validator, openapi_v3_spec_validator, openapi_spec_validator.validation.exceptions.OpenAPIValidationError, DuplicateOperationIDError, ExtraParametersError, ParameterDuplicateError, UnresolvableParameterError, ValidatorDetectError, OpenAPISpecValidatorError, openapi_core.OpenAPI.check_spec
  note    Where openapi-spec-validator 0.8.5 is silent and the specification is not, the specification's text is taken, with kin-openapi's error kinds: a requirement naming an undeclared scheme, a default outside its `enum`, two templates equal but for their names, a server variable its URL does not use, all problems here and none there; that validator's schema lacks a Link's `server`, which is read here, and raises on a reference to nothing, a problem here

